  "summary": "The Lean formalization accurately captures the 'Moreover' clause of Reinhardt's Theorem 3 (T ⊢ B(a) implies T ⊢ B(b)) in a sound first-order epistemic logic matching Reinhardt's B-axioms and optional B-prefixing of closed axioms without a general necessitation rule on T. The main caveats are the specialization of U(e, x) to a fixed atomic binary predicate and of p/q to the diagonal formula (aligned with the claim's 'for the same instance' qualification), together with the declared omission of arithmetic."
